WEBVTT

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:12.880
--Your Majesty!
--Your Majesty!

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:16.340
Your Majesty, punish the rebels
with force of arms!

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:20.600
Calm down! Are you certain that the
Duke of Buckingham leads the rebels?

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:22.270
We can't afford mistakes!

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:26.190
The rebels have proclaimed it,
and the duke hasn't denied it!

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:30.690
Your Majesty, Buckingham has declared
the Earl of Richmond his new king!

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:35.070
Richmond? Does he even
have a claim to the throne?

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:37.370
He comes of the Lancastrian royal line.

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:41.580
A new king?

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:46.080
But he... He was <i>my </i>kingmaker.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:50.840
King Richard, if His Grace truly
has joined the Lancastrians,

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:52.960
the boys in the Tower...

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:59.220
If the Lancastrian Richmond really
means to seize the crown,

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:02.100
then the next briar in his path will be...

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:05.520
He's had...

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:09.560
He's had more than enough time
to give me his answer.

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:13.860
If Richard can't cut through the briars,
then there's only one path.

00:01:14.990 --> 00:01:18.410
Like I did then,
I'll take it upon myself to...

00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:25.290
If I weren't king, I might have
run to you immediately.

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:31.040
I might have given up
everything without a thought.

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:34.090
But if I release my grip now...

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:39.470
--Your Majesty!
--Your Majesty!

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:42.390
Call soldiers!

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:46.850
Assemble our finest troops at once!

00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:52.730
York of the white rose.

00:01:52.730 --> 00:01:55.360
Lancaster of the red rose.

00:01:55.360 --> 00:02:01.780
These royal houses with roses for
their crests battled for the throne.

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:06.370
People call their strife
the "Wars of the Roses."

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:48.350
Your Majesty.

00:03:48.350 --> 00:03:51.060
I am the king.

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:55.400
Back then, I could have
thrown it all away.

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:57.570
But now...

00:03:57.570 --> 00:04:01.030
Sooner or later,
God will pass judgment on me

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:04.240
for forsaking my oath of love and trust.

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:11.160
Are you truly certain about this?

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:13.750
Was there any other way?

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:23.800
Are you saying that I should
never have become king?

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:27.640
If I had never lain with him...

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:30.520
If I weren't a demon child...

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:33.390
King Richard.

00:04:33.390 --> 00:04:37.020
Pondering what-ifs does no good.

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:40.360
Isn't that right, Henry?

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:44.150
I was able to grasp the light
because I had you with me.

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:48.370
I seized my desire with these hands.

00:04:48.370 --> 00:04:53.160
So, I will never allow this body
to rule my soul again.

00:04:55.870 --> 00:05:00.710
Catesby, go to London and fetch Jane.

00:05:00.710 --> 00:05:02.880
As fast as you can.

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:08.890
Northumberland,

00:05:08.890 --> 00:05:10.390
I'm glad you came.

00:05:10.390 --> 00:05:11.510
Your Majesty!

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:17.520
I... I'm a knight too! I'll fight!

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:19.400
Edward.

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:21.900
I'll help you, Father.

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:31.330
Going to war means killing others,

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:35.540
or sometimes dying before
you get a chance to fight.

00:05:35.540 --> 00:05:38.420
Battle is pointless and brutal.

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:44.760
Honor demands stifling your feelings
to fight in the reek of mud and blood.

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:46.050
Can you do that?

00:05:48.590 --> 00:05:52.510
I cannot take him into battle.

00:05:52.510 --> 00:05:55.850
Not this kind child.

00:05:55.850 --> 00:05:57.100
Father,

00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:59.940
this seems so painful for you.

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:02.900
So... So, I'll join you!

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:07.490
The king must fight.

00:06:08.530 --> 00:06:12.660
Even against friends and family
when they turn on him.

00:06:26.970 --> 00:06:32.600
Richard, I don't know what passed between
you and the Duke of Buckingham,

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:35.560
but I believe in you.

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:38.980
Both as a father and as a king.

00:06:38.980 --> 00:06:43.520
We shall march southwest
and strike the main rebel force!

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:46.070
Advance with all haste!

00:06:46.070 --> 00:06:47.070
Edward,

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:50.490
keep Anne safe for me.

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:56.870
Your Excellency, proceed as we planned.

00:06:57.870 --> 00:07:01.540
Days of rain have seriously delayed us.

00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:06.380
Now that we can't hope
to reach London ahead of him,

00:07:06.380 --> 00:07:09.130
we'll have to take that route.

00:07:09.130 --> 00:07:10.470
Richard,

00:07:10.470 --> 00:07:14.890
I'll march to the place
where we were to meet.

00:07:14.890 --> 00:07:20.020
Your Majesty, our scouts report that
Buckingham has already left his castle,

00:07:20.020 --> 00:07:22.690
but his destination remains unknown.

00:07:22.690 --> 00:07:25.360
Still, he can't march
quickly in this rain.

00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:28.070
The forest.

00:07:28.070 --> 00:07:34.280
True. He could enter the forest of Dean
and ford the river to reach London.

00:07:34.280 --> 00:07:38.750
I thought we had already
parted ways for good,

00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:40.960
and yet...

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:43.250
Give the order to our whole force!

00:07:43.250 --> 00:07:44.750
To the forest of Dean!

00:07:46.340 --> 00:07:50.420
I know where my other half will go.

00:07:50.420 --> 00:07:54.090
He's waiting for me in that forest.

00:07:56.180 --> 00:08:00.230
If we cut through the woods
and ford the river, London is ours!

00:08:01.230 --> 00:08:06.610
I don't care if I fall to earth or my good
name is dragged through the mud.

00:08:06.610 --> 00:08:10.780
I will end our kingdom
with my own two hands.

00:08:10.780 --> 00:08:13.660
Where are you, Buckingham?

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:16.370
Once we meet, it will all be over.

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:18.200
And yet...

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:21.660
Our scouts bring word!
Buckingham's army is in these woods!

00:08:23.540 --> 00:08:27.090
My frozen blood flows backwards.

00:08:27.090 --> 00:08:29.630
It cries out for that heat.

00:08:29.630 --> 00:08:31.380
Your Majesty!

00:08:31.380 --> 00:08:34.800
Your heat that burned away my curse.

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:38.260
Not even merciless
arrows of rain can quell it.

00:08:38.260 --> 00:08:41.140
My soul burns with longing.

00:08:41.140 --> 00:08:44.100
Even if it brings everything to an end.

00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:58.910
Half of my divided self
wails with desire for you.

00:09:03.290 --> 00:09:07.750
Buckingham, I cannot allow
you to reach London!

00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:11.250
Is that your answer?

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:12.630
If so...

00:09:18.850 --> 00:09:22.680
I must slay Richard III here and now.

00:09:22.680 --> 00:09:24.350
Your Majesty! Leave Buckingham to--

00:09:24.350 --> 00:09:27.350
Stay back!
I'll see to this personally!

00:09:27.350 --> 00:09:28.980
Come, Richard!

00:09:33.280 --> 00:09:34.490
Buckingham!

00:09:34.490 --> 00:09:36.320
You can't run forever!

00:09:38.490 --> 00:09:39.620
Buckingham!

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:43.410
Raise your sword.

00:09:43.410 --> 00:09:46.580
You mean to kill me, don't you?

00:09:46.580 --> 00:09:52.630
In that moment when your burning
golden eyes reflect only me...

00:09:56.340 --> 00:10:00.550
...supreme bliss lights my soul ablaze.

00:10:36.840 --> 00:10:40.890
I've never dreamed of killing you.

00:10:40.890 --> 00:10:43.300
--Then why--
--I want to kill...

00:10:44.680 --> 00:10:46.560
...King Richard III!

00:10:56.480 --> 00:10:59.280
Richard, it's not too late.

00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:03.780
Richard III could vanish here,
in the midst of battle.

00:11:03.780 --> 00:11:07.950
A little evidence left behind
would convince everyone

00:11:07.950 --> 00:11:10.460
that King Richard and
the Duke of Buckingham

00:11:10.460 --> 00:11:13.960
perished in the floodwaters,
still locked in combat.

00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:18.840
Is that why you led me
away from the troops?

00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:21.590
We'll go abroad and forsake our names.

00:11:21.590 --> 00:11:26.600
I'll stay at your side, clearing briars
from your path as long as I live.

00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:31.270
Even the loyalty to your father
that binds you now.

00:11:31.270 --> 00:11:33.650
Loyalty to my father?

00:11:33.650 --> 00:11:35.230
Yes.

00:11:35.230 --> 00:11:40.990
Your longing for the crown must have
its roots in your father's ambition.

00:11:42.410 --> 00:11:47.200
Was that truly your own wish?

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:54.580
It's true that I sometimes wondered
if my light lay elsewhere.

00:11:54.580 --> 00:11:58.590
But I only sought such salvation
because I had lost hope.

00:12:00.260 --> 00:12:01.930
Buckingham,

00:12:01.930 --> 00:12:05.680
you opened my eyes to the truth.

00:12:08.100 --> 00:12:12.270
Now that the light is mine, I know.

00:12:13.770 --> 00:12:16.860
My father's spirit is no briar.

00:12:16.860 --> 00:12:22.360
His wish, memory,
and suffering are all a part of me.

00:12:25.660 --> 00:12:28.450
Those are the thorns I mean.

00:12:28.450 --> 00:12:31.960
So are Anne, Edward, and all the rest.

00:12:31.960 --> 00:12:34.790
England, and even you.

00:12:34.790 --> 00:12:35.880
That's why...

00:12:37.670 --> 00:12:39.550
...I can't go with you.

00:12:41.380 --> 00:12:44.340
I have only one wish now!

00:12:44.340 --> 00:12:46.180
Flee, Henry!

00:12:47.680 --> 00:12:51.470
Flee in the boat I meant to take with you?

00:12:51.470 --> 00:12:53.850
Flee to a world without you?

00:12:55.940 --> 00:12:59.900
What would such a world be worth?

00:12:59.900 --> 00:13:03.490
It's the best we can do now.

00:13:03.490 --> 00:13:05.950
If we live, we have a future.

00:13:05.950 --> 00:13:10.200
No matter where you go,
I promise to find you and follow.

00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:11.450
Until I do,

00:13:11.450 --> 00:13:14.500
I'll think of this ring as you.

00:13:21.170 --> 00:13:23.260
Not a mere ring.

00:13:23.260 --> 00:13:28.010
If only I could sear
this kiss into your hand!

00:13:28.010 --> 00:13:30.510
A mark to remind you

00:13:30.510 --> 00:13:35.190
of these lips, which will always
call your name with love.

00:13:50.120 --> 00:13:55.540
Say no more, but swear you'll write to me.

00:13:57.170 --> 00:13:58.210
Your Majesty!

00:14:00.340 --> 00:14:03.130
Take this ring. It bears the royal seal.

00:14:03.130 --> 00:14:05.880
You'll find it useful in a tight spot.

00:14:05.880 --> 00:14:06.840
Go!

00:14:13.010 --> 00:14:14.180
Richard.

00:14:19.730 --> 00:14:22.270
Your Majesty!
The river has burst its banks!

00:14:22.270 --> 00:14:23.900
Fall back at once!

00:14:23.900 --> 00:14:26.110
The flood has scattered our foes.

00:14:26.110 --> 00:14:28.280
They won't be able to run far.

00:14:30.490 --> 00:14:32.410
It's fading.

00:14:32.410 --> 00:14:38.000
The cruel rain is stealing
the last vestige of warmth,

00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:43.590
as though it had all been an
illusion from the very beginning.

00:14:48.090 --> 00:14:49.010
Your Grace!

00:14:49.010 --> 00:14:50.340
You're unhurt!

00:14:50.340 --> 00:14:52.430
Let us retreat to a friendly manor

00:14:52.430 --> 00:14:55.310
and wait for the Earl of
Richmond's reinforcements!

00:14:55.310 --> 00:14:56.850
I'll fetch you a horse!

00:15:00.020 --> 00:15:01.810
Richmond won't come.

00:15:03.150 --> 00:15:06.440
A storm is delaying his forces.

00:15:06.440 --> 00:15:10.820
Those soldiers might
betray you if they knew.

00:15:10.820 --> 00:15:13.660
I wouldn't mind if they did.

00:15:15.290 --> 00:15:20.040
You called me a part of you.

00:15:20.040 --> 00:15:24.630
But to me, Richard, you are everything.

00:15:29.880 --> 00:15:31.720
Tyrrell, take this.

00:15:34.430 --> 00:15:37.180
I'll have no more need of it.

00:15:39.020 --> 00:15:42.020
I have one last duty to fulfill.

00:15:56.450 --> 00:15:59.540
I hear that His Majesty is in residence.

00:15:59.540 --> 00:16:01.370
Why, Sir Catesby!

00:16:01.370 --> 00:16:04.380
Inform the king that
I've returned from London.

00:16:04.380 --> 00:16:05.670
Make way!

00:16:05.670 --> 00:16:07.420
Hey, isn't that...?

00:16:10.630 --> 00:16:12.130
Buckingham?!

00:16:15.140 --> 00:16:16.760
How?

00:16:16.760 --> 00:16:19.810
His Grace seems quite resigned.

00:16:19.810 --> 00:16:25.060
I'm told that his comrades
sold him for a reward.

00:16:25.060 --> 00:16:28.110
It can't be. He should have
been able to escape.

00:16:28.110 --> 00:16:30.820
So, why is he...?

00:16:30.820 --> 00:16:33.780
Behead the traitors who gave him up.

00:16:33.780 --> 00:16:36.780
The rebel Buckingham deserved no better!

00:16:36.780 --> 00:16:39.540
Death is the only punishment for treason!

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:42.410
That's right.

00:16:42.410 --> 00:16:46.250
I've slaughtered countless
foes before now.

00:16:47.880 --> 00:16:51.800
It's only natural that he
would be no exception.

00:16:54.050 --> 00:16:56.090
Why, Henry?

00:16:56.090 --> 00:16:57.600
Why did you come back?

00:17:00.140 --> 00:17:03.480
Is this the ending King Richard wanted?!

00:17:03.480 --> 00:17:07.150
Continue to protect Richard
as you always have.

00:17:07.150 --> 00:17:09.110
I have another role.

00:17:09.110 --> 00:17:10.690
That's all.

00:17:10.690 --> 00:17:14.570
Your "role" is to betray him
and be executed?

00:17:16.070 --> 00:17:20.660
I wanted to obtain something at any cost.

00:17:20.660 --> 00:17:22.330
Ever since childhood.

00:17:22.330 --> 00:17:25.210
The two of us finally seized it.

00:17:25.210 --> 00:17:30.300
Because of that, I realized that we
had been looking at different lights.

00:17:31.130 --> 00:17:37.800
I shouldn't have to tell you that I take
what I want by any means necessary.

00:17:37.800 --> 00:17:42.270
You drew out his secret desires

00:17:42.270 --> 00:17:45.270
and cruelly led him down
a path of wickedness.

00:17:46.230 --> 00:17:49.730
Your sins are beyond forgiveness!

00:17:49.730 --> 00:17:50.860
True.

00:17:50.860 --> 00:17:53.150
And I won't change.

00:17:53.150 --> 00:17:58.280
As long as I live, I'll long to possess
Richard completely. I can't help it.

00:17:58.280 --> 00:18:01.870
If you realize that,
you could live on and atone!

00:18:01.870 --> 00:18:03.620
Don't play the saint!

00:18:03.620 --> 00:18:08.000
You would commit any heinous
crime for his sake as well.

00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:11.800
I know that I would kill
Richard if left unchecked!

00:18:14.340 --> 00:18:20.260
Even so, I still believe
that you should not die.

00:18:20.260 --> 00:18:28.100
If you imagine that I mean
to scar Richard with my death,

00:18:28.100 --> 00:18:30.690
you're mistaken.

00:18:30.690 --> 00:18:37.200
My role is to clear the briars
from Richard's path.

00:18:37.200 --> 00:18:41.070
Even if I turn out to be one of them.

00:18:42.450 --> 00:18:46.960
I doubt that I'll ever be able to
agree with your way of thinking.

00:18:48.250 --> 00:18:52.790
Does Your Grace have any last requests?

00:18:52.790 --> 00:18:55.420
Execute me soon.

00:18:55.420 --> 00:19:00.260
A long prison stay will
leave me dingy and haggard.

00:19:00.260 --> 00:19:02.930
I want to look my best for Richard.

00:19:04.060 --> 00:19:05.520
I'll inform him.

00:19:06.680 --> 00:19:10.020
Wait. Just one more thing.

00:19:10.020 --> 00:19:12.110
Enough. Say no more.

00:19:12.110 --> 00:19:14.730
--But--
--I don't want to hear any more!

00:19:14.730 --> 00:19:17.070
It's his final wish.

00:19:17.070 --> 00:19:20.410
He wants to see you one final time!

00:19:22.910 --> 00:19:26.490
Meeting him will blunt my resolve.

00:19:26.490 --> 00:19:31.330
Incompatible desires threaten
to tear my soul apart.

00:19:32.710 --> 00:19:34.630
King Richard.

00:19:34.630 --> 00:19:36.710
Where is she?

00:19:36.710 --> 00:19:39.220
You brought Jane, didn't you?

00:19:39.220 --> 00:19:41.470
Your Majesty summoned me?

00:19:41.470 --> 00:19:44.970
I've brought what you desire.

00:19:44.970 --> 00:19:47.270
Catesby, leave us.

00:19:48.430 --> 00:19:50.730
A drink of that will end it?

00:19:52.480 --> 00:19:57.570
I... I only wanted... to be king.

00:20:01.570 --> 00:20:04.450
No one's life is without regret.

00:20:07.370 --> 00:20:11.750
The date of Your Grace's
execution has been set.

00:20:11.750 --> 00:20:13.460
Tomorrow.

00:20:13.460 --> 00:20:17.130
Won't Richard come to see me?

00:20:17.130 --> 00:20:19.460
Tomorrow is All Souls' Day.

00:20:19.460 --> 00:20:23.300
We may pray for anyone's soul then.

00:20:23.300 --> 00:20:27.560
For friends, for foes,
and even for despicable traitors.

00:20:30.230 --> 00:20:36.150
Prayers? What could be less fitting

00:20:36.150 --> 00:20:38.650
for demons like us?

00:20:39.650 --> 00:20:41.740
No. You're...

00:20:41.740 --> 00:20:44.240
You're no demon!

00:20:44.240 --> 00:20:47.280
The only demon was me!

00:20:47.280 --> 00:20:53.370
God, if you exist, I'll spend
my last hours in prayer.

00:20:53.370 --> 00:20:55.790
Please, do not punish Richard.

00:20:57.340 --> 00:20:59.880
Your Grace, the Duke of Buckingham!

00:20:59.880 --> 00:21:02.090
Marriage? It's absurd.

00:21:02.090 --> 00:21:04.680
They were fighting to
the death not long ago.

00:21:04.680 --> 00:21:07.260
Now they make a show of merriment.

00:21:07.260 --> 00:21:11.140
This marriage is the end of my life.

00:21:11.140 --> 00:21:16.100
Living like a pet dog, with no will
of my own, is no better than death.

00:21:21.190 --> 00:21:23.280
Training at a time like this?

00:21:23.280 --> 00:21:25.110
Some noble's child?

00:21:25.110 --> 00:21:27.620
More importantly, are they a boy?

00:21:32.910 --> 00:21:34.250
Ow.

00:21:34.250 --> 00:21:36.250
Are you suicidal?!

00:21:36.250 --> 00:21:39.460
Duke Richard! The feast is beginning!

00:21:39.460 --> 00:21:40.630
I'll be there soon!

00:21:40.630 --> 00:21:42.090
H-Hey...

00:21:42.090 --> 00:21:45.050
Use your head more, damn brat.

00:21:45.050 --> 00:21:47.680
Don't die even if you are weak.

00:21:53.430 --> 00:21:54.980
Shameless wretch!

00:21:54.980 --> 00:21:56.480
Traitor!

00:21:56.480 --> 00:21:57.480
Traitor!

00:21:57.480 --> 00:22:01.570
I don't believe in God or fate.

00:22:02.980 --> 00:22:04.610
I have no regrets.

00:22:05.820 --> 00:22:08.910
I was born in this world
and got to meet you.

00:22:11.790 --> 00:22:14.450
I have nothing to say. Do it.

00:22:17.170 --> 00:22:21.170
But if I had one final wish...

00:22:25.470 --> 00:22:27.220
...it would be...

00:22:28.970 --> 00:22:32.810
It would be to see you... once more.

00:22:50.910 --> 00:22:51.870
Henry.

00:22:54.040 --> 00:22:57.000
Wait for me in hell.

00:23:00.080 --> 00:23:02.880
I swear that we'll meet again.

00:23:19.890 --> 00:23:24.360
This blood seals the pact

00:23:24.360 --> 00:23:26.530
that will reunite us.
